mkext2 produces images compatible with those of genext2fs / xgenext2fs, but
contains no code from them. Compatibility was obtained by a clean-room
process: the image generation engine was written from a behavioral
specification (docs/SPEC.md), and verified against the xgenext2fs program as
a black box. See CLEANROOM.md.

The tar reader (crates/mkext2/src/source/tar.rs) reproduces the behavior of
libarchive's tar format reader (https://www.libarchive.org, BSD 2-Clause
License, Copyright (c) Tim Kientzle and contributors).

The internal hash function implements the FxHash algorithm, as in the
rustc-hash crate (https://github.com/rust-lang/rustc-hash, MIT or
Apache-2.0).
